DAY 20 – FILE HANDLING AND FILE OPERATIONS

1. FILE HANDLING

File handling is used to create, read, write and
modify files using Python.

It allows programs to store and retrieve data
from files.


2. OPENING AND CLOSING FILES

Files are opened using the open() function.

After completing file operations, the file should
be closed.

Closing a file releases the resources used by it.


3. READING FILES

Python provides different methods for reading file data:

read() → Reads the file content.

readline() → Reads one line at a time.

readlines() → Reads all lines and returns them
as a list.


4. WRITING DATA

Writing is used to add data to a file.

The write() method is used to write data into a file.

Writing in write mode can replace existing content.


5. APPENDING DATA

Appending is used to add new data to the end
of an existing file.

Append mode preserves the existing content.


6. WITH OPEN()

The with open() statement is used for file handling.

It automatically closes the file after the
file operations are completed.

It is preferred because it manages the file
resource automatically.


7. FILE MODES

r → Read mode

w → Write mode

a → Append mode

r+ → Read and write mode

w+ → Write and read mode

a+ → Append and read mode


8. READ MODE – r

Used to read the contents of an existing file.

The file must already exist.


9. WRITE MODE – w

Used to write data into a file.

If the file already contains data, the existing
content can be overwritten.


10. APPEND MODE – a

Used to add data at the end of a file.

Existing content is preserved.


11. READ AND WRITE MODE – r+

Allows both reading and writing.

The file must already exist.


12. WRITE AND READ MODE – w+

Allows both writing and reading.

Existing content may be overwritten.


13. APPEND AND READ MODE – a+

Allows both appending and reading.

New data is added at the end of the file.


14. SENDING EMAILS USING PYTHON

Python can be used to send emails using
the smtplib module.

The EmailMessage class can be used to create
and manage email content.


15. SMTPLIB

smtplib is a Python module used for sending
emails using the Simple Mail Transfer Protocol (SMTP).

It can be used to connect to an SMTP server
and send emails.


16. EMAILMESSAGE

EmailMessage is used to create the content
and structure of an email.

It can contain information such as:

• Sender
• Receiver
• Subject
• Email body


17. GMAIL SMTP

Python can be used with Gmail SMTP for sending
emails.

The SMTP connection should be configured securely
when sending emails.


KEY TAKEAWAY

Python file handling allows programs to work
with files for storing and retrieving data.

read() → Reads file content.

readline() → Reads one line.

readlines() → Reads all lines.

w → Writes data.

a → Appends data.

with open() → Handles files and closes them automatically.

smtplib → Used for sending emails.

